e students, including tuition remission, fellowships without service requirements, or Student Academic Appointments (SAAs). SAAs, such as research, teaching, or graduate assistantships, are managed by individual programs\u2014not the Graduate School\u2014and typically provide a stipend, health and dental insurance, and tuition waivers. Additional SAA or hourly opportunities may be found through GradGrants, Handshake, or student affairs. Contact your graduate program for specific details on assistantships and other funding.\nIU Indianapolis graduate students can also access aid through the IU Indianapolis Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships. For graduate and professional student financial aid advice, email iuindy.finaid@iu.edu or call 317-274-4162.\nIf you are currently in the military, or a veteran please visit IU Indianapolis' Military-Connected Student Services to learn more about opportunities available to you.\nFellowship and Awards\nLearn about the various fellowships and awards offered through the IU Graduate School Indianapolis.\nGraduate Student Academic Appointments\nThe IU Indianapolis Office of Academic Affairs oversees the appointments process for SAAs, for more details visit their page.\nOffice of Scholar Development\nThe Office of Scholar Development (OSD) at Indiana University Indianapolis supports students who are interested in competitive national scholarships and grants.\nGraduate Student Loans\nLearn more about graduate student loans.\nMoneySmarts\nNeed to beef up your financial literacy quotient? Got a burning question about a specific money-related topic? Want to get your moneysmarts from the source? MoneySmart is where you can find answers.\nEmergency Funding\nAre you facing an unexpected financial challenge or nearing graduation with limited remaining funding? IU Indianapolis offers grant and loan funding to eligible students facing these situations.\nGradSense\nLearn what funding options are available for which degrees, plan your future with their debt to earnings calculator, and create a budget that will see you through your program.\nApply to graduate school\nIndiana Partner Tuition\nGraduate Programs\nGraduate Non-Degree Program\nFuture Student FAQs\nHow to Apply\nAbout IU Indianapolis\nVisit IU Indianapolis\nTuition & Fees\nTesting\nIndiana Partner Tuition\nFinancial Support\nFellowships & Awards\nTravel Fellowships\nStudent Loans\nTax Information\nIndiana University Graduate School Indianapolis resources and social media channels\nContact Us\nGive Now - support graduate students\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nAccessibility |\nCollege Scorecard |\nOpen to All |\nPrivacy Notice\n|\nCopyright \u00a9 2026\nThe Trustees of\nIndiana University", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/financial-support/index.html#content"], ["Skip to Main Navigation", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/financial-support/index.html#nav-main"], ["Skip to Search", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/financial-support/index.html#search"], ["Indiana University Indianapolis Indiana University Indianapolis IU Indianapolis", "https://indianapolis.iu.edu/index.html"], ["", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/admissions/search"], ["About", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/index.html"], ["Graduate School Events, Programs & Resources", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/gradoffprogs/index.html"], ["Student Spotlights", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/student-spotlights/index.html"], ["Student Awards", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/student-spotlights/student-awards.html"], ["Southern Regional Education Board (SREB) Doctoral Scholars", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/student-spotlights/sreb.html"], ["Commitment to Student Success", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/student-success.html"], ["Measures of Quality", "https://graduate.indianapolis.iu.edu/about/quality.html"], ["Student Demographics", "